IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`
IMPORT `g5-art13-effects`
IMPORT `g5-tests-fixtures`

-- g5-tests-art13-effects.l4: tests of Article 13(1) to (5), (11) and (13).  Every expected value was decided from the Law's text (quoted above each
-- group) before the run.  A DEONTIC has no equality, so each regulative rule is run with #TRACE and the expectation sits in an EXPECT comment right
-- above the trace (checked by check-traces.py): FULFILLED, BREACH or STANDING (the rule is printed back, still open).

§ `Tests of Article 13 (effects of registration), paragraphs (1) to (5), (11) and (13)`

§§ `Days and readings used below`

`the favoured reading` MEANS `the favoured interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`

`the day before the Arts Trust was registered` MEANS YMD 2019 2 28
`the day the Arts Trust was registered` MEANS YMD 2019 3 1
`a day while the Arts Trust was registered` MEANS YMD 2023 1 1
`a day long after registration, with no deregistration` MEANS YMD 2030 1 1
`the day before deregistration takes effect` MEANS YMD 2022 6 29
`the day deregistration takes effect` MEANS YMD 2022 6 30
`the day after deregistration takes effect` MEANS YMD 2022 7 1
`a day between the effective date and a later notice` MEANS YMD 2022 8 1

§§ `Article 13(1): while registered, and only until deregistered`

-- src:372 | (1) Paragraphs (2) to (4) apply while an entity is registered as a charity, and only cease to apply if the entity is deregistered.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day the Arts Trust was registered`
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day before the Arts Trust was registered`
-- "only cease to apply if the entity is deregistered": a charity never deregistered is still within it years later.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day long after registration, with no deregistration`
-- Deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022: the day before, applies; the day deregistration takes effect and after, reading A (taken): does not.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day before deregistration takes effect`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day deregistration takes effect`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day after deregistration takes effect`
-- Trap T15: a deregistration with retrospective effect under Article 17(3) takes effect "for all purposes" from the past date, so a day between that
-- past date and the notice is not a day of registration.  Here the date deregistered is the past date.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `a day between the effective date and a later notice`
-- Fork F5.6, reading B: the day deregistration takes effect is still a day of registration.
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the interpretation with the effective day inside the registration` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day deregistration takes effect`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the interpretation with the effective day inside the registration` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day after deregistration takes effect`
#ASSERT `Art 13(1) paragraphs (2) to (4) apply on the day` `the interpretation with the effective day inside the registration` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day before deregistration takes effect`
-- The two private readings, called directly.
#ASSERT `F5.6 A: the day is before the day deregistration takes effect` (YMD 2022 6 30) (YMD 2022 6 29)
#ASSERT NOT `F5.6 A: the day is before the day deregistration takes effect` (YMD 2022 6 30) (YMD 2022 6 30)
#ASSERT `F5.6 B: the day is not after the day deregistration takes effect` (YMD 2022 6 30) (YMD 2022 6 30)
#ASSERT NOT `F5.6 B: the day is not after the day deregistration takes effect` (YMD 2022 6 30) (YMD 2022 7 1)

§§ `Article 13(2): a provision that would let the purposes include a purpose that is not charitable`

-- src:373 | (2) Any provision of the entity’s constitution or constitutional Law is of no effect to the extent that it purports to permit an amendment of the purposes of the entity to include a purpose that is not charitable.
-- Purposes: a political purpose is not charitable (Article 6(5)), whatever head it might fall under; a purpose under a head of Article 6(1) is charitable;
-- the advancement of a philosophical belief is analogous to religion (Article 6(2)(f)) and so charitable.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `purpose to advance education`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `purpose to promote a candidate for election`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `purpose to educate voters for a candidate`
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `purpose to advance a philosophical belief`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is a charitable purpose` `purpose to run a members' social club`
-- A provision permitting a political purpose, while the Arts Trust is registered: of no effect.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
-- A provision permitting only a purpose under a head of Article 6(1): it has its effect.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education`
-- A provision permitting any purpose whatever includes non-charitable purposes: of no effect to that extent.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose`
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose that has a head`
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a social club`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a philosophical purpose`
-- "to the extent": a provision that permits both a charitable and a non-charitable purpose is of no effect as to the second.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting education and a political purpose`
-- A provision that is not part of the constitution or the constitutional Law is not one paragraph (2) speaks of.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision that is not part of the constitution`
-- Paragraph (2) applies only while registered (13(1)): before registration, and after deregistration takes effect, the provision is not of no effect by paragraph (2).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day before the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day after deregistration takes effect` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
-- Retrospective deregistration (trap T15): in the interval between the past date and the notice, paragraph (2) does not bite.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `a day between the effective date and a later notice` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
-- Fork F5.7: a purely ancillary purpose (Article 5(1)(a)(ii)).  Reading A (taken, literal): not a charitable purpose, so caught.  Reading B: not caught.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a purely ancillary purpose`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the interpretation with ancillary purposes not caught` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a purely ancillary purpose`
-- Under reading B a purpose that is neither charitable nor ancillary is still caught, and so is a political one.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the interpretation with ancillary purposes not caught` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a social club`
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the interpretation with ancillary purposes not caught` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
#ASSERT `F5.7 A: the purpose is not a charitable purpose under Article 6` `purpose to run a cafe`
#ASSERT NOT `F5.7 B: the purpose is neither charitable nor purely ancillary or incidental` `purpose to run a cafe`
-- A purpose that is both political and ancillary is not ancillary (Article 6(5)).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` `purpose to promote a candidate for election`

§§ `Article 13(13): paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order of the court under the Loi of 1862`

-- src:405 | (13) If a court-approved fidéicommis or an incorporated 1862 association becomes registered as a charity under this Law, paragraphs (2) and (3) do not apply to that registered charity to the extent that they are inconsistent with any order made, whether before or after registration under this Law, by the court under the Loi of 1862.
#ASSERT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the fideicommis charity` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the 1862 association charity` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
-- An order that is consistent leaves paragraphs (2) and (3) in force.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the fideicommis charity` `a provision permitting any purpose, with a consistent order under the Loi of 1862`
-- No order under the Loi of 1862: nothing to yield to.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the fideicommis charity` `a provision permitting any purpose`
-- Paragraph (13) speaks of those two kinds only: a trust registered as a charity does not get the benefit of it.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(13) paragraphs (2) and (3) yield to an order under the Loi of 1862` `the Arts Trust` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
-- The effect on paragraph (2): of no effect for the trust, not of no effect (to that extent) for the fideicommis and the 1862 association.
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the fideicommis charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the 1862 association charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT `Art 13(2) the provision of the constitution is of no effect` `the favoured reading` `the fideicommis charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with a consistent order under the Loi of 1862`

§§ `Article 13(3): a provision that would let a different charitable purpose be added or substituted`

-- src:374 | (3) Any provision of the entity’s constitution or constitutional Law that purports to permit an amendment of the purposes of the entity to add or substitute a different charitable purpose, is to be read as being subject to the entity –
-- src:375 | (a) providing evidence, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of a reason justifying the proposed amendment; and
-- src:376 | (b) obtaining the Commissioner’s prior approval of the proposed amendment.
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education`
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose`
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting education and a political purpose`
-- A provision that permits only a non-charitable purpose is not one paragraph (3) speaks of (it is paragraph (2)'s).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose`
-- Paragraph (3) is one of the paragraphs (2) to (4) that apply only while registered.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day before the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust, deregistered with effect from 30 June 2022` `the day after deregistration takes effect` `a provision permitting only education`
-- Article 13(13): an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862 displaces paragraph (3).
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the 1862 association charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862`
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) paragraph (3) applies to the provision` `the favoured reading` `the 1862 association charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with a consistent order under the Loi of 1862`
-- (a) and (b) are both required, "and": evidence and prior approval.
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education` FALSE FALSE
-- Where paragraph (3) does not apply, it asks nothing of the entity.
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day before the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting only education` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the 1862 association charity` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting any purpose, with an inconsistent order under the Loi of 1862` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 13(3) the amendment of purposes is subject to evidence and approval` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` `a provision permitting a political purpose` FALSE FALSE

§§ `Article 13(4): public benefit, and evidence for a request to amend the statement`

-- src:377 | (4) The entity must –
-- src:378 | (a) provide public benefit in accordance with its registered public benefit statement; and
-- src:379 | (b) if it requests the Commissioner’s approval of a proposed amendment to that statement, provide evidence, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of a reason justifying that request.
@ref Article 13 (src:377-379)
`the Arts Trust's registered public benefit statement` MEANS "The Trust gives free concerts to the public of Jersey"

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide public benefit in accordance with the registered public benefit statement` `the Arts Trust's registered public benefit statement` AT 30

-- Public benefit not in fact provided in accordance with the statement: the act of providing it does not count; the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide public benefit in accordance with the registered public benefit statement` `the Arts Trust's registered public benefit statement` AT 30

-- The duty has no time: with no act and the clock run on, the duty still stands (the Law states no period).
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Not while registered (13(1)): the duty does not arise.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(4) the registered charity must provide public benefit in accordance with its statement` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `the day before the Arts Trust was registered` TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- (b): a request for approval of an amendment to the statement; the evidence must satisfy the Commissioner.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` AT 10

-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `provide evidence of a reason justifying the request, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` AT 10

-- No request: the condition "if it requests" is not met; nothing is owed.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(4)(b) the registered charity that requests approval of an amendment of its statement must provide evidence` `the favoured reading` `the Arts Trust` `a day while the Arts Trust was registered` FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 13(5): the condition of the restricted section`

-- src:380 | (5) A registered charity must, while it is entered in the restricted section of the register, ensure –
-- src:381 | (a) that it meets the condition, prescribed under Article 9(2), as to which the Commissioner was satisfied under Article 9(6)(b); or
-- src:382 | (b) if, before it ceased to meet that condition, the Commissioner gave prior permission for it to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition prescribed under that Article, that it meets that condition as specified in that permission.
-- Reading A (taken).
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that still meets its condition and has no permission`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition and has no permission`
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition, with a prior permission, and meets the different condition`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition, with a prior permission, and fails the different condition`
-- A permission given only after the cessation is not "prior permission".
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition, with a permission given afterwards, and meets the different condition`
-- Fork F5.8: a prior permission exists, but the charity has not ceased to meet its original condition and fails the different one.
-- Reading A (taken): (a) alone suffices, so it complies.  Reading B: the different condition has replaced the original, so it does not.
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity with a prior permission that still meets its original condition and fails the different one`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity with a prior permission that still meets its original condition and fails the different one`
-- (b) is open to a charity that "ceased to meet that condition": one that never met it has not ceased to, so on reading A it cannot use (b); on reading B the permission governs.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the favoured reading` `a charity that never met its condition, with a prior permission, and meets the different condition`
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity that never met its condition, with a prior permission, and meets the different condition`
-- Where both readings agree.
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition, with a prior permission, and meets the different condition`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition, with a permission given afterwards, and meets the different condition`
#ASSERT `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section meets what paragraph (5) requires` `the interpretation with the permission replacing the condition` `a charity that still meets its condition and has no permission`

-- The duty arises only while the charity is entered in the restricted section.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition and has no permission` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- In the restricted section and meeting the condition: an act of ensuring it counts.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust, in the restricted section` `a charity that still meets its condition and has no permission` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `ensure that the charity meets the condition on which it is entered in the restricted section` AT 12

-- In the restricted section and not meeting the condition (nor a permitted one): an act of "ensuring" is not performance; the duty stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST
#TRACE `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `the favoured reading` TRUE `the Arts Trust, in the restricted section` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition and has no permission` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `ensure that the charity meets the condition on which it is entered in the restricted section` AT 12

-- An entity that is not a registered charity is not bound.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(5) the registered charity in the restricted section must ensure it meets its condition` `the favoured reading` FALSE `the Arts Trust, in the restricted section` `a charity that ceased to meet its condition and has no permission` AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

§§ `Article 13(11): payments inconsistent with the statement of intentions; permission to amend it`

-- src:401 | (11) A registered charity –
-- src:402 | (a) must not make any payment that is inconsistent with a statement provided under paragraph (9)(b);
-- src:403 | (b) may apply to the Commissioner, with reasons, for permission to amend that statement.
-- A payment inconsistent with the statement: a breach, whenever it is made (the prohibition has no time).
-- Arguments: the interpretation; the entity is a registered charity; an Order under Article 13(9) applies to it.
-- EXPECT: BREACH Article 13(11)(a)
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment inconsistent with the statement of intentions` AT 400

-- A consistent payment is no breach: the prohibition stands.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST NOT
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment consistent with the statement of intentions` AT 400

-- No statement has been provided: nothing for the payment to be inconsistent with.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST NOT
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment when no statement has been provided` AT 400

-- A statement provided only after the payment (1 June 2023, the payment being of 10 May 2023) cannot bind the payment.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MUST NOT
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment made before any statement was provided` AT 400

-- No Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity: there is no statement, so no prohibition.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment inconsistent with the statement of intentions` AT 400

-- An entity that is not a registered charity is not bound.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(a) the registered charity must not make a payment inconsistent with its statement` `the favoured reading` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `make a payment` `a payment inconsistent with the statement of intentions` AT 400

#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment inconsistent with the statement of intentions`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment consistent with the statement of intentions`
-- Fork F5.14.  A payment that contradicts the first statement but fits the amended one of 1 February 2023: reading A (taken), the statement in force is the
-- amended one, so it is consistent; reading B, it is inconsistent with a statement provided.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`
-- A statement provided on the day of the payment counts (it is "on or before" that day), under either reading.
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment on the day a contradicting statement was provided`
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` `a payment on the day a contradicting statement was provided`
-- A statement provided after the payment counts under neither reading.
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment that contradicts only a later statement`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` `a payment that contradicts only a later statement`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment made before any statement was provided`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the interpretation with any statement provided` `a payment made before any statement was provided`
#ASSERT NOT `Art 13(11)(a) the payment is inconsistent with the statement` `the favoured reading` `a payment when no statement has been provided`
-- The statements provided on or before the day of the payment (a statement provided on the day itself counts).
#ASSERT count (`Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` `a payment that fits the amended statement but not the first`) EQUALS 2
#ASSERT count (`Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` `a payment that contradicts only a later statement`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT count (`Art 13(11)(a) the statements provided on or before the day of the payment` `a payment made before any statement was provided`) EQUALS 0
-- The Law states no penalty for the prohibition: no imprisonment and no fine (it is not an offence).
#ASSERT `Art 13(11)(a) the penalty for a payment inconsistent with the statement` EQUALS `Penalty provided` OF NOTHING, `no fine is provided`

-- (b): the charity may apply, with reasons.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions` "the planned works cost more than expected" AT 7

-- An application with no reasons is not the application the paragraph describes.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions` "" AT 7

-- A permission not used is not a breach.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- No statement provided: nothing to amend.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(b) the registered charity may apply for permission to amend the statement` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `a registered charity` DOES `apply to the Commissioner for permission to amend the statement of intentions` "the planned works cost more than expected" AT 7

§§ `The Commissioner's approvals and permissions (implied by Article 13(3)(b), (4)(b), (5)(b) and (11)(b))`

-- src:376 | (b) obtaining the Commissioner’s prior approval of the proposed amendment.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(3)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of purposes` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give an approval or permission` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)` AT 20

-- Without a proposal there is nothing to approve.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(3)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of purposes` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- Nobody is acting as the Commissioner: no permission is available.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(3)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of purposes` FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give an approval or permission` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)` AT 20

-- Approval is a permission, not a duty: unexercised, the permission is not a breach.
-- EXPECT: STANDING MAY
#TRACE `Art 13(3)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of purposes` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(4)(b) the Commissioner may approve the proposed amendment of the statement` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give an approval or permission` `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)` AT 20

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(5)(b) the Commissioner may give prior permission to remain in the restricted section` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give an approval or permission` `prior permission to remain entered in the restricted section on the basis of a different condition, Article 13(5)(b)` AT 20

-- A charity in the general section has nothing to remain entered in the restricted section on.
-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(5)(b) the Commissioner may give prior permission to remain in the restricted section` TRUE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    (`WAIT UNTIL` 4000)

-- EXPECT: FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 13(11)(b) the Commissioner may give permission to amend the statement` TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the Commissioner` DOES `give an approval or permission` `permission to amend the statement of intentions as to payments, Article 13(11)(b)` AT 20

-- Integration point IP27: the decision as a record of subject and outcome.
#ASSERT `Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `approval of a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)(b)` TRUE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the charity's purposes, Article 13(3)`, outcome IS `the Commissioner does what was sought or proposed`
#ASSERT `Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `approval of a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)` FALSE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS `whether to approve a proposed amendment of the registered public benefit statement, Article 13(4)(b)`, outcome IS `the Commissioner refuses`
#ASSERT `Art 13 the decision of the Commissioner` `permission to amend the statement of intentions as to payments, Article 13(11)(b)` FALSE EQUALS `Decision of the Commissioner` WITH subject IS `any other matter`, outcome IS `the Commissioner refuses`
